er  they told me horror stories about  children that had fallen off the train  children that disappeared while they  were on the road with them that this is  a real humanitarian crisis  but i thought what was more interesting  was that the children  actually knew president biden i asked  them  do you know who the president of the  united states is they said  yes of course it's president biden and  they misinterpreted his stop on  deportations  uh for 100 days as being an invitation  to arrive to the united states they said  that the  human traffickers the cartels the people  that were moving them into the united  states  basically said it was about a hundred  days to get here  to freedom so that they once they got  here they would have amnesty  these kids were willingly turning  themselves into border patrol  i can't tell you how heartbreaking it is  though when you know that none of these  the children at least that i spoke to  had seen doctors  many of them said that their parents  were still back in honduras  that they were trying to find family  here in the united states and that their  parents sent them ahead of them  some of these children we don't even  know if they were actually traveling  with their actual parents we actually  believe that they may be  traveling with strangers that their  parents were paid  to bring them on this journey i spoke  with chris cabrera  he is the national border patrol council  vice president president for the union  and here's what he had to say as a bp  agent what goes through your mind when  you see this when you see  this influx of young people and know  that they have traveled like probably  one of the most dangerous routes  to get to the united states it's  heartbreaking to see that you know i  mean  you think about these kids what they go  through on the journey  how many of these kids don't make it how  many how many how many don't make it  the full journey because there's nobody  there watching out for them what's in  their best interest  what kind of surge are you expecting  this year yeah we're expecting thousands  a day  right now we're between 700 and a  thousand daily  and we're seeing that number increase  for the most part daily i mean it ebbs  and flows  but it's steadily increasing and the  unique part is  years ago this was just something that  we dealt with in the rio grande  not the rest of the united states and  now we're seeing it from the rio grande  valley sector all the way to san diego  it's happening all over the border  they're coming in large groups in laredo  in in big bend in el paso and arizona  huge groups are coming in  because they know that they're going to  be let go and once they get here no  matter  what they hear our politicians say if  our politicians say don't come right now  well we'll send you back it's as long as  one person gets through  they call back home and said this is  what we did we got through and more are  going to follow what i would tell  president biden or anybody else in  up in dc that has any type of authority  is  this needs to stop being a partisan  issue i'm not saying that it's partisan  issue on him i'm just saying  in general you know with the republicans  the democrats  if you want to solve this problem you  have to leave your partisan hat at the  door they have a  fence around the capitol now i mean so  if it's if it's good for these folks it  should be good for  the rest of america it should be for our  country  yeah sean i mean the crisis couldn't be  any worse they say they're expecting  these numbers to increase by the  thousands  uh come springtime there's a lot of  concern here about where they're going  to house these children  and more and more undocumented children  are coming across the border we're also  seeing a lot of family units  and there's a big concern here as well  with the spread of covid  and the fact that the majority of people  coming through are not being tested  and remember the dhs secretary sarah  said we want you to come but just don't  come right now  so to be clear these these families  with children and it's tragic it's  tragic this is a perilous journey a  one where people are dying making this  journey  uh they feel there's an open invitation  by the president of the united states to  come  a and b they still won't let you get  inside the cargo ship containers  uh with the little window with bars on  it you have no access to that you have  tried correct  absolutely we've tried correct and we  have not heard a response back from the  dhs  i can tell you this that dhs secretary  mallorcas  a lot of people are very concerned uh  about the message that he's putting  across about the message that there  isn't a crisis  i can tell you that the border patrol  agents here in the rio grande valley  sector  are doing a tremendous job they're doing  everything they can to stop this flow  and by the way  they're doing everything they can to  comfort these children and at the same  time fend off the drug cartels  there's no doubt that these are real  heroes on on the u.s mexico border here  okay sarah thank you
 

